[wolfer@cbnewse.ATT.COM also ponders:]
>[Excalibur] started out +0, but when I read a scroll of Enchant Weapon,
>it went up to +3.

in nh3 you should get familiar with the blessed/cursed state of items.
as an example an uncursed scroll of enchant weapon will provide 1
enchantment to your wielded weapon when read and remove a curse if
necessary. a blessed scroll of enchant weapon works better in that it
provides 3 enchantments and possibly blesses the weapon as well. a
cursed scroll of enchant weapon provides -1 enchantment. the
blessed/cursed state is significant with things like potions of
invisibility, gain ability, monster detection and gain level and scrolls
of genocide, identify, enchant armor or weapon. also blessed weapons
work better against the undead ...

[dbekker@CIE.UOREGON.EDU additionally questions:]
>off the subject, in area of level 14-16 i often mysteriously get polymrphed
>into something. this is a real pain! why and how does this happen?
if it really is a mystery then i'll rule out a ring or amulet of
polymorph or that you polymorphed yourself somehow. stepping on a
polymorph trap usually has the effect of turning you into some monster.
it appears that these traps don't show up as often early in the dungeon.
if you are wearing a ring of polymorph control you can indicate a
preference for what monster you'd like to become. turning into certain
monsters has an unfortunate side effect, as you know, on your armor.
becoming a master lich or vampire lord, for example, isn't risky in that
regard. if you are magic protected, i.e. you're wearing appropriate armor
like the wizard's cloak, the polymorph trap won't effect you. searching
or detecting unseen in the vicinity of the trap could reveal it's
presence before you activate it. fare thee well ...

